      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cr and V segregate to grain boundaries and triple junctions in the baseline W38Ta36Cr15V11 alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding Hf will alter elemental segregation at grain boundaries and triple junctions.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf will reduce Cr and V mobility and clustering by acting as a diffusion barrier.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf has lower diffusivity and a high mixing enthalpy with the refractory elements in this alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Hf-induced changes in defect-migration kinetics will stabilize the solid solution and prevent Cr and V from forming second phases during irradiation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy will show a significant reduction or complete absence of Cr-V-rich precipitates at approximately 8 dpa and 1073 K.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline W38Ta36Cr15V11 alloy has strong radiation resistance, including no observed irradiation-created dislocation loops after 8 dpa.",
      "field": "baseline",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC6397024::web::000::abstract",
        "PMC6397024::web::017::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The baseline W38Ta36Cr15V11 alloy demonstrates practical bulk manufacturability.",
